s unit ends up as waste, costing about 7 plus roughly 9 in storage. A missing unit costs 14, so ordering 1.0× and 1.1× the forecast come out roughly even. What tips it to candidate 7 is the day-4 cash squeeze, where it keeps 30–35 more units than candidates 5 and 6.\n- My rough estimate is that candidate 7 beats candidate 6 by about 700 in expectation and candidate 5 by about 1,000. Candidates 2 and 1 (1.2× and 1.3×) are worse: more waste and a cancelled day-4 order.\n\n**Every-other-day plans (0 and 3):**\n- With the forecast exactly right, candidate 0 makes about 9,900 against about 11,630 for candidate 7. Ordering on half the days saves about 640 in daily fees.\n- That saving is eaten by storage on two-day batches (about 1,190 in total), the cut day-4 order (47 units of product 0 and none of product 1) and storage overflow at the 236 limit on days 24–28. Overflow costs about 50 units of product 1. Product 0 is also left over at the end (about 62 units).\n- With random demand, candidate 0 still trails candidate 7 by about 600. Candidate 3 orders more, so it has less cash on day 4 and more overflow, and it is no better.\n\n**Ranking:** 7 > 6 ≈ 5 > 4 > 0 ≈ 3 > 2 > 1."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3941, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3941}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T02:28:25.537Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAoTksvWtekr7dq1FHix"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01UqRP93pLi